<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
===============================================================================
AERIS — Smart Building AI Dashboard
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This HTML file is the frontend of the project.

Main responsibilities:
1. Show the user interface for the smart building system.
2. Let the user choose room, date, and prediction model.
3. Send requests to n8n workflows through webhooks.
4. Receive prediction/anomaly/recommendation results.
5. Display the results using cards, charts, and readable messages.

Important:
- HTML builds the structure.
- CSS controls the design.
- JavaScript handles logic and communication with n8n.
===============================================================================
-->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<!--
===============================================================================
HEAD SECTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This section contains page setup:
- Character encoding
- Responsive screen scaling
- Page title
- Google fonts
- Chart.js library
- CSS styling
===============================================================================
-->
<!-- Allows the page to display normal text, symbols, and special characters correctly. -->
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<!-- Makes the dashboard responsive on laptops, tablets, and phones. -->
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
<!-- Browser tab title. -->
<title>AERIS — Smart Building AI Platform</title>
<!--
Google Fonts:
Inter is used for clean dashboard text.
JetBrains Mono is used for technical/number-like labels.
-->
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<!--
===============================================================================
CHART.JS LIBRARY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This bundled library is used to draw temperature and humidity charts.
The library code is kept unchanged because it is third-party code.
===============================================================================
-->
